00:10:47.382 --> 00:10:48.870
(tense music)

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:52.020
As for the Beltracchis,
despite the background story,

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.270
some questions still continue to pop up

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.690
regarding the mysterious Jager Collection.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.420
Some buyers begin asking for documentation

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.180
that could support the
history of the collection

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.610
or they want to see some sort of proof

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.480
of Werner Jager's ties
to Alfred Flechtheim.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.060
Everyone wanted to believe the story,

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.270
but some piece of hard
evidence would seal the deal.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.549
And so Wolfgang and Helena
come up with a simple solution.

00:11:19.549 --> 00:11:21.270
(tense music continues)

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:24.630
Wolfgang prints out copies
of several of his paintings

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.360
that have already been sold,

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:31.050
and next he frames them
on a wall in his kitchen.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.180
Then Helena dresses herself

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:36.900
in the clothes of her
grandmother, Josephina Jager,

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.480
and she poses in front of the paintings,

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.210
sitting at an old kitchen table.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.610
Wolfgang then takes her photograph

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:46.560
using a time-authentic camera

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.870
and making sure it's slightly out of focus

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.340
to help hide the fact that

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.730
the woman in the photo is actually Helena.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.650
Then Wolfgang prints the picture

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.230
on old pre-war developing paper,

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.270
and the result is this.

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:03.654
(tense music ends)

00:12:03.654 --> 00:12:06.000
A fake family photo that looks like

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.370
it could be from the 1930s,

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.705
while in reality, it
was taken in the '90s.

00:12:11.705 --> 00:12:12.630
(pensive music)

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:15.120
This painting on the left
side of the photograph

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:19.110
is actually a fake
imitation of Fernand Leger,

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:23.640
and this one on the right
is a fake Max Ernst.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.940
This staged photograph eases
any doubts that were had

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.947
about the authenticity
of the Jager Collection,

00:12:28.947 --> 00:12:32.580
and Wolfgang is able to
continue creating more paintings

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.090
that will be sold by
Helena, Jeanette, and Otto,

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:39.180
as the Beltracchis are amassing a fortune.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.763
- At 80,000? 82,000?

00:12:41.924 --> 00:12:43.511
84,000 pounds?

00:12:43.511 --> 00:12:44.610
(gavel thuds)

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.370
- [Narrator] That is until 2006,

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.494
when everything would change.

00:12:49.494 --> 00:12:50.970
(pensive music)

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.330
It all starts with another
Heinrich Campendonk forgery,

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.580
as Wolfgang is putting
the finishing touches

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.565
on a piece he calls "Red
Picture with Horses."

00:12:59.565 --> 00:13:00.750
(pensive music continues)

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.540
This time, the title of
the painting is real,

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:07.290
but the actual painting
itself has been lost to time.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.120
After finishing his rendition of

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.460
what he thinks the
painting would look like,

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.710
it's time to pass it off.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.630
This time, Jeanette will be the one

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:18.780
taking the painting to a
prestigious art gallery

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:22.440
and "Red Picture with
Horses" proves to be a hit.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.690
A Maltese company, Trasteco,

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:27.270
has placed a winning bid on the painting

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:30.633
and they pay over $3
million for their prize.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.170
So far, nothing seems out of the ordinary,

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:36.270
at least until the company asks for

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.190
a certificate of authenticity,

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.623
which, of course, doesn't exist.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.580
Since the auction house cannot
provide the certificate,

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.960
Trasteco decides to have

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.360
their own analysis done on the painting,

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.120
and they are put in touch
with Andrea Firmenich,

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:52.950
the same Campendonk expert

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:56.910
who has previously been fooled
by Wolfgang's forgeries.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.400
But this time with so
much money on the line,

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.590
Firmenich decides to take extra measures

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.126
to make sure that the painting is genuine.

00:14:04.126 --> 00:14:05.850
(suspenseful music)

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.370
She begins with the closest she has

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:12.240
to a certificate of authenticity, a label.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.070
Fixed to the back of the painting

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.980
that claims it is from the
Alfred Flechtheim collection,

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.810
there is a small label,

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:21.780
and has the artist Heinrich
Campendonk's signature

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.300
with a sketched photo
of Flechtheim beneath,

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.944
acting as his seal for his collection.

00:14:26.944 --> 00:14:28.140
(suspenseful music continues)

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.840
Firmenich then reaches
out to Ralph Jentsch,

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.570
an expert on the life
of Alfred Flechtheim,

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:37.230
to help in determining if
this label is legitimate.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:39.450
And as soon as Jentsch sees the label,

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.280
he can't help but feel bewildered

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:44.880
that anyone would ever
take it to be genuine.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.550
He has seen the real Flechtheim labels

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:49.830
and the silly caricature on this one

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.860
is an instant giveaway that it isn't real.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.530
He is convinced and lets Firmenich know

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:58.320
that the label is a forgery.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:00.420
Now that she knows she's on the trail

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.360
of exposing "Red Picture
with Horses" as a fake,

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.640
Firmenich decides to
send the actual painting

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:07.710
for scientific analysis,

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:10.350
and the results are equally as damning

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:12.543
as history repeats itself.

00:15:13.794 --> 00:15:15.270
(bright music)

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.070
When the German police investigated

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.620
the fake Molzahn
paintings in the nineties,

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.650
they found out that a
color pigment had been used

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.730
that simply wasn't available
when it was supposedly created.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:31.140
And this time in 2006, again,
scientific analysis reveals

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.760
that this painting as well

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:36.030
contains a special
pigment, titanium white,

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.783
which did not exist when the
painting was supposedly done.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.390
And so in the coming years,

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:45.445
the house of cards begins to fall.

00:15:45.445 --> 00:15:48.090
Firmenich takes her
findings back to Trasteco,

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.250
the company that purchased the painting,

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.010
and almost immediately,
a civil trial begins

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.073
to recover the $3 million
from the auction house.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:58.343
At the same time,

00:15:58.343 --> 00:16:00.900
Ralph Jentsch begins
scouring the art world

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.430
to uncover more paintings

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:05.100
marked with the same label on the back.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:09.210
And in just two weeks, he
comes up with 15 paintings,

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.970
all supposedly from the Jager Collection,

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.313
bearing the fake Flechtheim label.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:16.950
And with more scrutiny,

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:21.840
the story Helena once gave
also begins to fall apart.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:25.230
It turns out that Werner
Jager was just a teenager

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.990
when Flechtheim's gallery was ceased.

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.930
And to make the story
even more implausible,

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.510
Jager grew up to join the Nazi Party,

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.400
making it incredibly unlikely

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:38.703
he would've befriended a
Jewish man like Flechtheim.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:43.620
With the evidence stacking
up of a major fraud scandal,

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:46.950
Ralph Jentsch takes his
findings to the German police,

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.448
and a criminal case is opened.

00:16:49.448 --> 00:16:50.640
(suspenseful music)

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.860
Through investigation,
police find out that

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.367
that the auction house had acquired

00:16:54.367 --> 00:16:57.360
"Red Picture with
Horses" through Jeanette.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.590
They also discovered that

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:02.490
her sister Helena has delivered
paintings in the past.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.080
They then begin wiretapping

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.090
the phones of Helena and Jeanette,

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:10.170
and for the first time learn
of the existence of Wolfgang,

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:14.310
realizing that he is at the
center of these fake paintings.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:16.230
And with enough evidence collected,

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.330
the German police want to make a move

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.460
on Wolfgang and Helena's estate.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.570
(suspenseful music continues)

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:23.670
But since it is located in France,

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.880
they need the cooperation
of the French authorities.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.100
But the French court is on vacation

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:32.880
and no one is available to
help the case move forward.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.400
Nevertheless, the German
police discovered that

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.040
Wolfgang and Helena also
own property in Germany

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.960
in the city of Freiburg.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.450
They find a large modern villa

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.298
spanning over several floors on a hill.

00:17:45.298 --> 00:17:47.130
(suspenseful music continues)

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.450
And not soon after,

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:51.509
Wolfgang and Helena venture
on a trip to this home.

00:17:51.509 --> 00:17:53.370
(suspenseful music continues)

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.790
With weapons drawn, police stop their car

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:59.250
and order them out into the rain.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.470
Wolfgang and Helena are arrested

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.510
and their children are left behind

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:05.910
with no idea what's going on.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.790
Police also arrest
Helena's sister Jeanette,

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.690
as well as Otto, the other
friend helping the operation.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:13.980
And though the evidence seemed to

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.620
stack up against Wolfgang and his cohorts,

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.753
there was one major problem.

00:18:19.882 --> 00:18:21.600
(suspenseful music)

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.820
The courts couldn't prove without a doubt

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:25.350
that Wolfgang was the one

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:28.170
who was actually creating
the fake paintings.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:30.900
And rather than risk
taking the case to trial,

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:34.980
both sides decided to
come to a plea agreement.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.250
All four accused pled
guilty to charges of fraud

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.830
for 14 forged paintings.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:42.930
Though the real number of paintings faked

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.850
is believed to be way higher,

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.570
as it is likely that there are
hundreds more still out there

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:51.240
that have yet to be discovered.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.060
Wolfgang is sentenced
to six years in prison,

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.850
Helena and Otto are given four years each,

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.643
and Jeanette is given
a suspended sentence.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.730
They are all allowed to
serve their sentences

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:03.990
in an open prison,

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.350
meaning they can still work
during the day five days a week

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:10.315
and return to prison every night.

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:13.530
(pensive music)

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.390
After serving his sentence

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.400
and being released early on parole,

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:21.270
Wolfgang returns to the
world as a mixed figure.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:24.900
Some see him as a hero
exposing the art world

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:28.800
and exposing the experts
as fake and superficial.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:31.500
Others point out that he
didn't commit the fraud

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:32.970
to make a statement,

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.100
but rather as a self-serving way

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:37.255
to make a profit for himself.

00:19:37.255 --> 00:19:38.760
(bright music)

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.770
Today, the notoriety that came

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:43.140
surrounding Wolfgang's
time as an art forger

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.780
has kept him in the spotlight.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.580
- What you do is horrible.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.900
Ripping off geniuses

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:52.230
who spent years perfecting their styles.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.150
- You only cared about that painting

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:57.450
when you thought it was
created by someone famous.

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.920
- [Narrator] And all the press coverage

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.400
made him a successful
artist in his own right.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.900
Wolfgang still paints,

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:08.220
and now Wolfgang signs his
paintings under his own name

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.235
and he seems to be
enjoying his newfound fame.

00:20:11.235 --> 00:20:12.810
(bright music continues)

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.970
Wolfgang's life has all the pieces

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.730
you'd expect from a great story.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.680
A person with a rare talent,

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:22.680
a partner who stood by his
side through everything,

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.000
the two of them plotting

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:27.840
one of the biggest art world
hoaxes in modern history.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.170
It's a love story, a crime story,

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.900
a story about exposing the art world

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:36.630
and getting away with it for years.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.820
And even when they were finally caught,

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:41.490
the ending wasn't some big downfall.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:44.760
They did their time, but
today they live in comfort,

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.303
painting what they want
without having to hide anymore.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:52.890
But if you're looking for
the arc of personal growth,

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.340
the kind that turns a
trickster into something more,

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:57.903
you won't find it here.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:02.070
Because it's impossible to say,

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:05.580
did Wolfgang expose the
greed of the art world

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.170
or did he simply take advantage of it

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:09.753
to satisfy his own greed?

00:21:13.682 --> 00:21:16.682
(bright music ends)

